  (text "Rails: B+1 +370 (reservoir · OT centre tap) · B+2 +368 (post-choke: 6V6 screens through their own 470 Ω · 1 W, and both halves of the tremolo bottle) · B+3 +310 (12AY7 plate loads · phase-inverter plate-load junction) · bias line -28 V off a -69 V rectifier" (at 12.7 252.528 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left)) (uuid "2acfc301-85d8-5508-a4f3-7971912c4787"))
  (text "Each volume control is driven at its WIPER, one end grounded and the other on the shared mixing node — the drawing's own arrangement, on both its pages. The tone control's wiper sits on that same node." (at 12.7 256.928 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left)) (uuid "fa097550-1ef2-58eb-9bc6-78a87e093f9b"))
  (text "Heaters, PT primary/mains, fuse, pilot lamp, the mains capacitor and the tremolo footswitch jack are omitted here — see the netlist, the sources list and the board drawing. The tremolo bottle IS drawn; only its DC operating point is excluded from the netlist (see the circuit story)." (at 12.7 261.328 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left)) (uuid "cb9774b3-208c-5952-aacc-7dcdb3395f4d"))
